file tools/t/tame_style_long_fn_witness.rish read back out; gates the control, both elder patterns' absence, and a floor of one on the tree's own reading
file tools/fixtures/t/tame_style_long_fn_one.sh read back out; brace depth read from code alone, with a named 4096-line bound
file tools/fixtures/t/tame_style_long_fn_scan.sh read back out; the walk and the rank, printing functions_over_70 and longest ahead of the top ten
file tools/fixtures/t/tame_style_long_fn_control.sh read back out; twenty behaviors in a pen, three of them biting the elder awk on the same fixture
file tools/t/two_rooms_doorway.rish read back out; the scan's output printed before any assert
file tools/fixtures/t/two_rooms_doorway_roster.sh read back out; the shell glob replaced by git ls-files, whose pathspec asterisk crosses a slash
file tools/fixtures/t/two_rooms_doorway_control.sh read back out; fourteen behaviors, ten flipping under the elder roster
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri both guards rostered at tier cadence, each with the cost that chose the clock
file construction/REDS.md the headline moved 509 to 511 and re-measured by the monotone witness rather than counted by hand
file README.md the fascia grade regenerated to what the repaired ledger actually reads, 68 down to 58
file construction/archive/20260906-204500_itinerary-landed-accounts.md the closed half folded off the card, which went over its bound when a peer landed a new account mid-send
file construction/ITINERARY.md the live front rewritten on today's bytes, the over-70 ratchet moved 14 to 321, the repaired sibling find retired
file session-logs/date/20260906/20260906-173013_the-record-and-the-ledger.kyri corrected before landing: it too died before its commit, and its rows renumbered a second time
recommend keep-going -- both reds close at this commit and the box is empty. The nearest honest lap in my lane is the card's own carried find: 890 depth-lost links in the two-level fold rooms, a refusal nothing tracked can read, and the same narrowed-reach class this pair just named twice. Two doors are not mechanical: dated_path_witness reds at refs_lost=166 against a ceiling of 165 while its scan prints no list, so nobody can name the reference; and the operator card took a fold this round rather than a sixth condensing pass -- two ships wrote new accounts inside one hour, the live front went 381 bytes over, and my own closed half went to its own shelf so the card kept only the live question. Eight ships at 2,048 apiece is the arithmetic that bound was derived from, and it is now the binding constraint on every send.
